<section>
  <h2>Open-source &amp; upstream</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Linux kernel (linux-wireless):</strong> authored the
      RTL8922AU USB RF-calibration fix
      (<a href="https://lore.kernel.org/linux-wireless/20260416045536.817930-1-loukot@gmail.com/">v3
      on lore</a>) merged into Ping-Ke Shih&rsquo;s
      <code>rtw-next</code> tree in April 2026, with five independent
      <code>Tested-by</code> tags across USB WiFi chipsets. Also a
      <a href="https://lore.kernel.org/linux-wireless/20260414122728.92234-1-loukot@gmail.com/">cfg80211
      MLO group-key error-message grammar fix</a> (Accepted by Johannes Berg).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>NetworkManager:</strong> authored Wi-Fi 7 MLO awareness for
      the daemon&rsquo;s background-scan logic
      (<a href="https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/NetworkManager/NetworkManager/-/merge_requests/2405">MR
      !2405</a>, merged July 2026): parses the AP-MLD address from the
      Multi-Link element so a single-AP MLO association keeps the relaxed
      scan cadence, eliminating scan-induced traffic stalls. Landed after
      a five-revision review with the core maintainers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>wireless-regdb audit:</strong> five country regulatory-database
      patches (ZA, HK, RU, KR, UA) verified against primary sources (ICASA, OFCA,
      MSIT, SCRF, ETSI), all merged into <code>wens/wireless-regdb</code> in
      April 2026. Plus a <code>Reviewed-by</code> on a community-submitted
      RU 6 GHz 320 MHz patch, applied to <code>wens/wireless-regdb</code> master
      on 2026-04-30: six total commits across five jurisdictions in one month,
      including first review credit on someone else's regulatory analysis.
      <a href="https://lore.kernel.org/wireless-regdb/?q=f:loukot@gmail.com">Patch
      series on lore.</a> Includes an audit script for ongoing monitoring.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>morrownr/rtw89:</strong>
      <a href="https://github.com/morrownr/rtw89/pull/76">PR #76</a> backports
      the in-kernel RF-calibration fix to the out-of-tree DKMS driver
      (merged April 2026).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fedora bug 2458629:</strong>
      <a href="https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2458629">filed
      a reproducer and root-cause analysis</a> for a wpa_supplicant MLO
      reassociation race; assigned, in triage.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>In review:</strong> 7 further patches across
      <code>wpa_supplicant</code> (hostap) and linux-wireless, covering
      Wi-Fi 7 MLO association fixes and EHT capability advertising.
      <a href="https://lore.kernel.org/all/?q=f:loukot@gmail.com">All
      submissions on lore.</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
